1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:08,335
Four systems. One customer. Your store, inventory, CRM and support desk each hold a piece of the same person.

2
00:00:09,185 --> 00:00:15,351
A customer updates their email in your store, but support still has the old one. Which is right?

3
00:00:16,201 --> 00:00:26,377
The fix: each piece of data has one owner. Orders in the store, stock in inventory, contact details in the CRM. The others read from the owner.

4
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:35,163
Then sync on events. When an order is placed or a ticket opened, the change reaches the other systems as it happens.

5
00:00:36,013 --> 00:00:42,562
The result: support sees the order, sales sees the ticket, and nobody copies data between tabs.

6
00:00:43,412 --> 00:00:53,097
